-- 0164: near-synonym sets for كِتَاب، قَابِل، إِلَٰه، مَصِير (Ghāfir 40:2–3) — checked and promoted (near_B).
-- near_B: near-synonym (furūq, 80-KIN) sets for the Ghāfir 40:2–3 words قَابِل (قبل), إِلَٰه (اله), مَصِير (صير)
-- and ٱلْكِتَٰب (كتب). Same shape as 0140. Every member checked against al-Rāghib, Ibn Fāris, Lane (English) and,
-- where the lexicons are silent, the tafsīr (al-Zamakhsharī, al-Ṭabarī, Ibn ʿĀshūr, al-Rāzī, al-Ālūsī); every
-- claim_text is cut verbatim from its block (checked by script); every evidence word checked against
-- qr_word_occurrence.gid_lemma (23/23 match the member lemma id).
--   كتب  FRQ:SET:kataba_writing (was 'manual', staging LEM:LEX:* ids): كَتَبَ, خَطَّ→تَخُطُّ, سَطَرَ→يَسْطُرُ promoted;
--        نَسَخَ → moved to Form X اسْتَنْسَخَ (نَسْتَنسِخُ 45:29): in the Qurʾān Form I يَنسَخُ means "cancel/remove"
--        (al-Rāghib p.801), not "copy". NOT promoted: زَبَرَ, رَقَمَ — no Qurʾānic verb (only زُبُر/زَبُور, مَرْقُوم/رَقِيم).
--   كتب  FRQ:SET:kitab_names ('direct_source', not shown): كِتَاب, قُرْءَان, زُبُر promoted; ذِكْر was UNSOURCED —
--        now sourced (al-Rāghib p.328); added فُرْقَان (al-Rāghib p.632; Lane p.2385).
--   قبل  NS:TO:TO_ACCEPT (AI draft, staging ids, combined labels «قَبِلَ-تَقَبَّلَ», «أَجَابَ-اِسْتَجَابَ»):
--        member X7EC0FF5E → قَابِل (passage lemma); X19F55FCD → اسْتَجَابَ; added تَقَبَّلَ, أَخَذَ, تَلَقَّى.
--        The combined staging lemmas are left unmerged (no single canonical twin).
--   اله  no fitting set (NS:DEITY:DEITY holds forgiveness words; NS:STATUS:STATUS_AND_CAPACITY left alone) →
--        NEW FRQ:SET:ilah_rabb: إِلَٰه, اللَّه, رَبّ, مَلِك (al-Rāghib pp. 82, 336, 774; Lane p.83; al-Rāzī on 114:1–3).
--   صير  NS:END:END_RESULT_CONSEQUENCE (AI draft): مَصِير, عَاقِبَة, مُنتَهَى filled; added مَرْجِع, مَآب;
--        rejected حَوَايَا and أَمْعَاء (no book ties them to an "end"). Staging ALL:NS:B301FCDFFF977D88 (مُنْتَهَى)
--        merged into canonical 840346c1466bb58781c9aa6954. صَارَ in NS:TO:TO_RETURN is untouched.
-- Tafsīr chunk_id = the QR block id (as 0140); note_md also carries 'QR:TE:<id>'. al-ʿAskarī's al-Furūq is not in the corpus.
UPDATE ar_ling_root_lemma_furuq_set SET canonical_en = 'Words for writing', canonical_ar = 'كَتَبَ · خَطَّ · سَطَرَ · اسْتَنْسَخَ', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'FRQ:SET:kataba_writing';
